Z||000010||william_thorniii||01-09-2000||06:46 PM||||Monkey, <P>Although Ogre in his infinite wisdom (All Hail the Great Ogre!) is correct, usually the drive couplers upon discintigration end up in the geartrain.  Which is precisely what causes the gears to get stripped.  Once I get my metal gears, I will give you my nylon ones.  They are in relatively good condition and might help you a few years down the road.  Actually I could give them to you now since they are just sitting on my bench downstairs.  <P>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||10
Z||000012||Monkeyman||01-09-2000||10:32 PM||||Thanx, William.  I'd appreciate it.  I'll get them when I bring your stuff to you.||||reg||1
